1
00:00:01,067 --> 00:00:06,600
["You're my favorite song"
BY PRINCESS ALIYAH]

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:10,167
<i>Previously
on You're my favorite song...</i>

3
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:12,433
<i>You know, it should've been you</i>

4
00:00:12,567 --> 00:00:14,800
<i>who died instead of Mom,
the one who truly loved me.</i>

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,933
<i>And my baby would still be alive</i>

6
00:00:20,067 --> 00:00:23,200
<i>if Dad hadn't cast me aside
along with Beverly.</i>

7
00:00:23,333 --> 00:00:23,933
<i> Where are you go...</i>

8
00:00:24,067 --> 00:00:25,067
<i>Why did you destroy our resort?</i>

9
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,900
<i> Yeah. Who are you?</i>

10
00:00:27,033 --> 00:00:29,867
<i>You know, he's one of the people
who wrecked our resort.</i>

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,833
<i>Kaila, do you know
where I can find them?</i>

12
00:00:31,967 --> 00:00:33,900
<i>I need to find out
why they did it</i>

13
00:00:34,067 --> 00:00:36,133
<i>and why they destroyed
our resort,</i>

14
00:00:36,267 --> 00:00:39,200
<i>or whether someone ordered them
to do it.</i>

15
00:00:39,333 --> 00:00:40,567
<i> Are you a Siklab fan?</i>

16
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:41,667
<i> They're okay.</i>

17
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:43,333
<i> Their songs are good too,</i>

18
00:00:43,467 --> 00:00:46,500
<i>but I like your original songs
even more.</i>

19
00:00:46,633 --> 00:00:49,600
<i>The thing about my dad is,
he's very controlling.</i>

20
00:00:49,733 --> 00:00:51,667
<i>He takes creative
control of my work.</i>

21
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:52,833
<i> Sorry, what was that?</i>

22
00:00:52,967 --> 00:00:54,600
<i> Oh, nothing. It's nothing.</i>

23
00:00:54,733 --> 00:00:57,633
<i> And the QuizCon continues!</i>

24
00:00:57,767 --> 00:00:58,933
<i> It'll be unstable.</i>

25
00:00:59,067 --> 00:01:00,633
<i>One small movement
and we'll tip over.</i>

26
00:01:00,767 --> 00:01:02,367
<i> You think you know everything.</i>

27
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:03,533
<i> You don't.</i>

28
00:01:03,667 --> 00:01:05,900
<i>I know what I'm doing
because I'm better than you.</i>

29
00:01:06,933 --> 00:01:07,967
<i> Go!</i>

30
00:01:08,133 --> 00:01:10,033
<i> Go, Brighton!</i>

31
00:01:10,167 --> 00:01:11,667
<i>- Go, Calix!
- Go, Angel!</i>

32
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:13,167
<i>- Go!
- Angel!</i>

33
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:15,267
<i> Calix, go!</i>

34
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:16,567
<i> I told you we'd sink.</i>

35
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:18,333
<i>See? We're the only ones
who sank.</i>

36
00:01:18,467 --> 00:01:19,467
[WATER SPLASHES]

37
00:01:21,033 --> 00:01:22,400
<i>It's just a competition, Angel.</i>

38
00:01:22,533 --> 00:01:23,833
<i> Move on.</i>

39
00:01:23,967 --> 00:01:26,300
<i>If you're fighting for yourself
and your image,</i>

40
00:01:26,433 --> 00:01:28,767
<i>I'm fighting for my grandfather.</i>

41
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:31,767
<i>That prize money would've
been such a huge help</i>

42
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:33,933
<i>with my grandfather's
hospital bills.</i>

43
00:01:34,067 --> 00:01:36,167
<i>That's why I agreed
to be your partner.</i>

44
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:38,100
<i>All you ever think
about is yourself.</i>

45
00:01:40,833 --> 00:01:47,967
<i>♪ 'Cause baby you are
my favorite song ♪</i>

46
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:51,467
<i>♪ I'll put you on repeat
all night ♪</i>

47
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:55,533
<i>♪ I know that
I'll never move on ♪</i>

48
00:01:55,667 --> 00:01:59,000
<i>♪ My first right
where I belong ♪</i>

49
00:01:59,133 --> 00:02:05,667
<i>♪ You are my first
heartbeat song ♪</i>

50
00:02:11,033 --> 00:02:17,633
Siklab!

51
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:20,133
[CHEERING]

52
00:02:20,267 --> 00:02:21,133
[SIKLAB SINGING "UNFORGETTABLE"]

53
00:02:21,267 --> 00:02:24,233
<i> ♪ Sometimes I think of you ♪</i>

54
00:02:25,533 --> 00:02:28,200
<i> ♪ Especially when I'm alone ♪</i>

55
00:02:29,667 --> 00:02:32,900
<i>♪ Especially when I have nothing
to do ♪</i>

56
00:02:33,033 --> 00:02:35,633
<i>♪ I'll never grow tired of it ♪</i>

57
00:02:35,767 --> 00:02:36,767
Siklab!

58
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:41,100
<i> ♪ After all this time ♪</i>

59
00:02:41,233 --> 00:02:45,233
<i>♪ Things are probably different
now ♪</i>

60
00:02:45,367 --> 00:02:49,533
<i>♪ But no matter how many years
pass, ♪</i>

61
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:53,433
<i>♪ I'll still find my way back
to you ♪</i>

62
00:02:53,567 --> 00:02:57,867
<i> ♪ I can't forget the joy, ♪</i>

63
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:01,633
<i>♪ every memory comes rushing
back ♪</i>

64
00:03:01,767 --> 00:03:03,533
<i> ♪ So many beautiful... ♪</i>

65
00:03:03,667 --> 00:03:06,367
Randel, Miguel looks exhausted
right now.

66
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:07,567
You didn't even
fix his appearance.

67
00:03:10,233 --> 00:03:12,267
Sir Neil,

68
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:14,433
please try to understand,

69
00:03:14,567 --> 00:03:17,200
the kid is completely drained.

70
00:03:17,333 --> 00:03:20,700
They've been doing nonstop
local tours with Siklab.

71
00:03:20,867 --> 00:03:24,800
And we still have international
tour dates to announce.

72
00:03:26,433 --> 00:03:29,333
Randel, as Miguel's manager,

73
00:03:29,467 --> 00:03:31,867
your job is to make sure
he looks good

74
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,533
in front of his fans!

75
00:03:33,767 --> 00:03:36,667
Not to keep giving me
unsolicited advice.

76
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:40,000
I'm sorry, Sir.

77
00:03:40,133 --> 00:03:43,433
<i>♪ Things are probably
different now... ♪</i>

78
00:03:43,567 --> 00:03:46,333
[CRICKETS CHIRPING]

79
00:03:46,467 --> 00:03:56,433
[MELLOW MUSIC]

80
00:04:08,367 --> 00:04:09,867
It's okay, Angel.

81
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,500
You've been crying
all afternoon.

82
00:04:11,633 --> 00:04:12,933
Your eyes will get swollen.

83
00:04:14,933 --> 00:04:16,133
Thank you, Zion.

84
00:04:19,733 --> 00:04:21,600
I'm thinking of selling
my tablet

85
00:04:21,733 --> 00:04:24,667
so I can come up
with 15,000 pesos tonight.

86
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:28,867
I desperately need it right now,
Zion.

87
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:37,500
Well...

88
00:04:37,633 --> 00:04:40,800
But, Angel, you need that
for school.

89
00:04:40,933 --> 00:04:43,333
How are you supposed
to study without it?

90
00:04:44,867 --> 00:04:47,500
And wasn't one of your
grandfather's

91
00:04:47,633 --> 00:04:49,333
bucket-list dreams...

92
00:04:49,467 --> 00:04:51,733
to see you graduate
with highest honors?

93
00:04:52,567 --> 00:04:54,200
I wish I could get a loan.

94
00:04:56,433 --> 00:04:58,967
But I'm only 16 years old, Zion.

95
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:04,300
You know, what if we
just try my suggestion?

96
00:05:04,467 --> 00:05:06,433
So, have you practiced?

97
00:05:06,567 --> 00:05:08,433
You mean...

98
00:05:08,567 --> 00:05:12,133
You know, that online
asking-for-donations thing.

99
00:05:12,267 --> 00:05:14,967
You know what,
I watched one before,

100
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:17,767
and people were incredibly
generous.

101
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:22,633
One time, someone
gifted 40,000 coins.

102
00:05:22,767 --> 00:05:26,133
That's worth around
30,000 pesos once converted.

103
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:28,467
There, you're smiling now.

104
00:05:30,033 --> 00:05:33,833
You know, crying really
doesn't suit you, Angel.

105
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:37,367
That's only for losers like me.

106
00:05:38,967 --> 00:05:40,267
Come on, Zion.

107
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,533
You're not a loser.

108
00:05:42,767 --> 00:05:45,833
I'm just thinking
that if we do that,

109
00:05:45,967 --> 00:05:48,867
our classmates will just make
even more fun of us.

110
00:05:53,033 --> 00:05:56,067
Why would they?

111
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:58,500
What we're doing is honest,
isn't it?

112
00:05:58,633 --> 00:06:00,833
We're not even wearing
our school uniforms.

113
00:06:02,733 --> 00:06:03,700
Besides...

114
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:06,933
you'll have me with you.

115
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:08,567
Right? If we embarrass
ourselves,

116
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:10,500
at least we'll go through it
together.

117
00:06:11,567 --> 00:06:12,433
So, are you in?

118
00:06:12,567 --> 00:06:14,200
Come on, let's try it.

119
00:06:14,333 --> 00:06:15,133
Just practice, okay?

120
00:06:15,267 --> 00:06:17,167
Let's pretend it's five each.

121
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:18,567
Okay, here. I'll put it here.

122
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:24,433
There, see?

123
00:06:24,567 --> 00:06:25,267
Right here.

124
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:30,300
Okay. So let's pretend
it's a rose first.

125
00:06:30,433 --> 00:06:36,700
- Rose, rose, rose, rose, rose.
- Rose, rose, rose, rose.

126
00:06:36,833 --> 00:06:37,967
Now coffee.

127
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:39,533
Five times.

128
00:06:39,667 --> 00:06:44,667
Coffee, coffee, coffee, coffee,
coffee.

129
00:06:44,833 --> 00:06:45,967
Oh, last one.

130
00:06:46,100 --> 00:06:47,000
Heart.

131
00:06:47,133 --> 00:06:53,100
Heart, heart, heart, heart,
heart, heart.

132
00:06:56,067 --> 00:06:58,833
Zion, thank you,

133
00:06:58,967 --> 00:07:01,733
for being willing to
embarrass yourself for me.

134
00:07:01,867 --> 00:07:02,800
Of course.

135
00:07:05,367 --> 00:07:07,433
I'd do anything for you, Angel.

136
00:07:07,567 --> 00:07:09,200
["FIRST LOVE" INSTRUMENTAL]

137
00:07:09,333 --> 00:07:10,900
[ANGEL EXHALES DEEPLY]

138
00:07:11,033 --> 00:07:13,133
Should we start the livestream?

139
00:07:13,267 --> 00:07:14,933
You in?

140
00:07:15,100 --> 00:07:16,533
I'm in.

141
00:07:16,667 --> 00:07:18,067
For my Grandpa Xavi.

142
00:07:19,367 --> 00:07:20,733
That's right.

143
00:07:20,867 --> 00:07:23,333
For your Grandpa Xavi.

144
00:07:23,467 --> 00:07:24,433
Ready?

145
00:07:24,567 --> 00:07:25,267
I'll start it now.

146
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:26,200
Let's do it.

147
00:07:28,067 --> 00:07:29,167
And three...

148
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:30,967
[GRUNTS]

149
00:07:31,100 --> 00:07:32,033
Wait a second.

150
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:35,300
Three...

151
00:07:37,633 --> 00:07:38,533
Two...

152
00:07:42,033 --> 00:07:43,567
One...

153
00:07:45,933 --> 00:07:47,167
There.

154
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:48,633
I thought we were starting?

155
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:53,900
It doesn't look like
it's started yet, Zion.

156
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:57,533
Well...

157
00:07:57,667 --> 00:07:59,667
Do you really think I'd let you
embarrass yourself

158
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:01,767
on that TokiToki livestream?

159
00:08:02,867 --> 00:08:08,400
["FIRST LOVE" BY HEATH,
CLIFFORD, AND MARCO]

160
00:08:08,533 --> 00:08:09,200
What's this?

161
00:08:09,333 --> 00:08:12,100
<i> ♪ How have you been? ♪</i>

162
00:08:12,233 --> 00:08:14,733
[SIKLAB SINGING "UNFORGETTABLE"]

163
00:08:14,867 --> 00:08:18,633
<i>♪ Things are probably different
now ♪</i>

164
00:08:19,633 --> 00:08:27,100
Siklab!

165
00:08:27,267 --> 00:08:29,933
[AUDIENCE SCREAMING]

166
00:08:33,333 --> 00:08:41,833
Miguel!

167
00:08:42,900 --> 00:08:44,733
[AUDIENCE CLAMORING]

168
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:52,500
Are you okay?

169
00:08:52,633 --> 00:08:53,400
Are you okay?

170
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:09,333
What's this?

171
00:09:11,967 --> 00:09:13,567
These are tickets to
Siklab's concert

172
00:09:13,700 --> 00:09:15,433
here in Solmera City next month.

173
00:09:17,900 --> 00:09:19,067
Come on, take them.

174
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:22,167
These are so hard to get, right?

175
00:09:22,300 --> 00:09:23,667
Exactly.

176
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:26,233
We can definitely sell these

177
00:09:26,367 --> 00:09:28,933
for more than 15,000 pesos,
right?

178
00:09:29,100 --> 00:09:30,433
Come on, take them.

179
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:34,233
You know, I stayed up nights
for those

180
00:09:34,367 --> 00:09:35,433
and saved up for them too.

181
00:09:36,967 --> 00:09:38,067
Well...

182
00:09:39,833 --> 00:09:42,167
I was planning
to give them to Charm.

183
00:09:42,300 --> 00:09:44,600
She's a huge Siklab fan, right?

184
00:09:44,733 --> 00:09:46,300
And she has the biggest crush
on Miguel.

185
00:09:47,233 --> 00:09:48,867
[ADIE AND CHARM SQUEAL]

186
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,000
<i> Oh, my gosh.</i>

187
00:09:50,133 --> 00:09:51,100
<i> He's so handsome!</i>

188
00:09:51,233 --> 00:09:53,567
<i>I want to see Miguel in person
at their concert</i>

189
00:09:53,700 --> 00:09:55,233
<i>- here in Solmera City.
- What?</i>

190
00:09:55,367 --> 00:09:56,833
<i>- He's so handsome, Adie.
- Oh, my God.</i>

191
00:09:56,967 --> 00:09:58,300
<i>- Oh, my gosh.
- Wait.</i>

192
00:09:58,433 --> 00:09:59,867
<i> Charm, your test paper.</i>

193
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,500
<i>Eighty-five out of one hundred.</i>

194
00:10:01,667 --> 00:10:02,667
<i> We got the same score.</i>

195
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:04,133
[TENSE MUSIC]

196
00:10:04,267 --> 00:10:05,233
<i> Thank you.</i>

197
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:08,267
<i> Loser.</i>

198
00:10:12,467 --> 00:10:15,567
I was just thinking,
if I gave those to her,

199
00:10:15,700 --> 00:10:18,700
maybe she'd give me a chance
too.

200
00:10:25,633 --> 00:10:27,533
Zion, I can't accept these.

201
00:10:27,667 --> 00:10:29,733
This is your chance
to be with Charm.

202
00:10:30,867 --> 00:10:32,433
- Come on, take them.
- Angel.

203
00:10:32,567 --> 00:10:34,533
Angel, don't.

204
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:37,233
There'll be plenty of chances
for me to ask Charm out.

205
00:10:38,967 --> 00:10:42,000
But your Grandpa Xavi's life,
you only get one of those.

206
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:43,967
So they're yours.

207
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:49,100
Zion, thank you.

208
00:10:51,833 --> 00:10:59,133
["FIRST LOVE" INSTRUMENTAL]

209
00:11:03,033 --> 00:11:06,033
I promise I'll pay you back,
even if it's triple the amount,

210
00:11:06,167 --> 00:11:08,733
once our resort
starts making money.

211
00:11:11,233 --> 00:11:16,767
[ZION STAMMERS]

212
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:18,567
[ZION CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY]

213
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:22,133
Ready?

214
00:11:23,833 --> 00:11:25,867
Well, let's go live.

215
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:31,700
Not to embarrass ourselves,
but to find a new buyer.

216
00:11:32,700 --> 00:11:33,533
So, shall we?

217
00:11:35,533 --> 00:11:36,700
Okay, I'm starting now.

218
00:11:52,233 --> 00:11:53,933
The patient is stable now.

219
00:11:54,067 --> 00:11:56,233
He can go home after two days.

220
00:11:56,367 --> 00:11:56,800
Thank you.

221
00:11:56,933 --> 00:11:57,933
Thank you, Doc.

222
00:11:58,067 --> 00:11:59,133
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

223
00:11:59,267 --> 00:12:00,567
- Thank you.
- Excuse me.

224
00:12:00,700 --> 00:12:01,533
Yes.

225
00:12:03,467 --> 00:12:05,100
[BEBE SIGHS]

226
00:12:05,233 --> 00:12:08,100
My child,
you still haven't told me

227
00:12:08,233 --> 00:12:10,967
where you got the money
we used to pay for this.

228
00:12:12,567 --> 00:12:15,367
It was Zion,
my friend from school.

229
00:12:15,533 --> 00:12:18,067
He helped me come up
with the money.

230
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:23,500
[SOFT MUSIC]

231
00:12:23,633 --> 00:12:24,633
There.

232
00:12:24,767 --> 00:12:26,400
We're live now.

233
00:12:26,533 --> 00:12:27,667
Hi, guys.

234
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:29,000
Guys, start claiming.

235
00:12:29,133 --> 00:12:31,967
We have tickets here
for the Siklab concert.

236
00:12:32,100 --> 00:12:34,533
Go ahead. Just leave a comment,
guys.

237
00:12:34,667 --> 00:12:35,533
Come on.

238
00:12:35,667 --> 00:12:37,167
No fake buyers, okay?

239
00:12:37,300 --> 00:12:38,600
Go ahead and claim them now.

240
00:12:38,733 --> 00:12:40,133
That's two tickets
right there.

241
00:12:40,267 --> 00:12:42,233
[CELLPHONE CHIMES]

242
00:12:42,367 --> 00:12:43,567
Okay.

243
00:12:43,700 --> 00:12:44,767
We've got comments.

244
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:45,833
Hi, guys!

245
00:12:48,467 --> 00:12:49,833
Guys, claim them now. Come on.

246
00:12:51,533 --> 00:12:52,900
Zion, someone paid.

247
00:12:53,033 --> 00:12:53,767
What?

248
00:12:53,900 --> 00:12:55,933
Someone sent money
to my e-wallet.

249
00:12:56,067 --> 00:12:56,933
Let me see.

250
00:12:58,700 --> 00:13:00,600
[CELLPHONE CHIMES]

251
00:13:01,067 --> 00:13:03,500
- Hi, guys.
- Zion, someone already paid.

252
00:13:03,633 --> 00:13:05,567
Someone sent money
to my e-wallet.

253
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:07,167
[ZION CHUCKLES]

254
00:13:07,300 --> 00:13:08,967
No way!

255
00:13:09,100 --> 00:13:10,667
- Let me see.
- Here.

256
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:12,100
[CELLPHONE CHIMES]

257
00:13:14,267 --> 00:13:15,233
Hey.

258
00:13:15,367 --> 00:13:17,033
It's Mr. Moon.

259
00:13:17,167 --> 00:13:18,267
Mr. Moon.

260
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:19,733
Mr. Moon, hi.

261
00:13:19,867 --> 00:13:21,233
- Hi, Mr. Moon.
- Mr. Moon.

262
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:24,000
Just send me a private message
so you can claim the tickets.

263
00:13:24,133 --> 00:13:25,700
We can definitely
arrange a meetup.

264
00:13:25,833 --> 00:13:28,233
Oh, thank you so much, Mr. Moon.

265
00:13:28,367 --> 00:13:29,500
- Mr. Moon, hello.
- Thank you.

266
00:13:29,633 --> 00:13:30,700
- Thank you, Mr. Moon.
- Thank you.

267
00:13:30,833 --> 00:13:32,567
Just send me a message.

268
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:34,167
- Thank you so much.
- Bye, Mr. Moon.

269
00:13:34,300 --> 00:13:36,200
Oh, thank you so much.

270
00:13:36,333 --> 00:13:37,567
Okay, guys,
I'm ending the stream now.

271
00:13:41,267 --> 00:13:42,400
That was so fast.

272
00:13:44,767 --> 00:13:46,367
Wow.

273
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:47,333
Nice.

274
00:13:47,467 --> 00:13:48,167
High five.

275
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:49,233
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

276
00:13:54,667 --> 00:13:56,433
[BEBE SIGHS HEAVILY]

277
00:13:56,567 --> 00:13:58,967
My child, thank you,
thank you so much.

278
00:14:03,533 --> 00:14:06,433
You know, I feel so ashamed.

279
00:14:07,333 --> 00:14:11,900
You shouldn't be carrying
such a heavy burden

280
00:14:12,033 --> 00:14:14,233
and such a huge responsibility.

281
00:14:15,233 --> 00:14:15,767
[GENTLE MUSIC]

282
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:17,933
Mama Bebe.

283
00:14:18,067 --> 00:14:22,200
You know I would never
let you drown in debt.

284
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:27,733
You raised me and loved me
as if I were your own child.

285
00:14:30,367 --> 00:14:33,200
Honestly, that's the least
I can do in return.

286
00:14:36,333 --> 00:14:39,467
[ANGEL SNIFFLES]

287
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:43,533
Just always remember that
I love you very, very much.

288
00:14:49,367 --> 00:14:51,000
I love you very much too.

289
00:15:28,733 --> 00:15:32,867
Calix, how come you've dropped
to rank two at Brighton?

290
00:15:33,633 --> 00:15:35,167
What the hell have you been
doing?

291
00:15:41,300 --> 00:15:42,467
There's a new student, Mom.

292
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,833
So, you're admitting
she's better than you?

293
00:15:48,567 --> 00:15:49,433
[SCOFFS]

294
00:15:49,567 --> 00:15:51,367
That's so embarrassing, Calix.

295
00:15:52,867 --> 00:15:55,867
Your brother Andrei is top
of his class in medical school.

296
00:15:56,900 --> 00:15:59,733
Jameson is top of his class
at law school in New York.

297
00:16:02,367 --> 00:16:05,500
And I heard you lost
at the Regional QuizCon.

298
00:16:06,567 --> 00:16:07,900
Your boat sank?

299
00:16:09,367 --> 00:16:12,133
It was like a school project.

300
00:16:12,267 --> 00:16:14,300
It was so simple, Calix.

301
00:16:14,433 --> 00:16:17,000
Yet you still couldn't get
your calculations right.

302
00:16:18,167 --> 00:16:20,500
[STUDENTS SHOUTING]

303
00:16:20,633 --> 00:16:23,167
[ROUSING MUSIC]

304
00:16:23,967 --> 00:16:28,533
<i>Unfortunately, Brighton's
boat has collapsed...</i>

305
00:16:28,667 --> 00:16:32,100
<i> Holy Crest!</i>

306
00:16:39,467 --> 00:16:40,967
I'll do better, Mom.

307
00:16:42,533 --> 00:16:43,500
Andrei.

308
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:47,700
I'll get my grades
back on track.

309
00:16:49,033 --> 00:16:49,833
You should.

310
00:16:51,967 --> 00:16:52,867
Also...

311
00:16:57,767 --> 00:17:03,600
Explain to me what
that 15,000 peso withdrawal

312
00:17:03,733 --> 00:17:05,033
from your bank account was for.

313
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:09,367
What did you use it for, Calix?

314
00:17:10,533 --> 00:17:11,967
You think I wouldn't notice?

315
00:17:16,900 --> 00:17:18,033
<i>Hey, the base,
the base, the base.</i>

316
00:17:18,167 --> 00:17:19,200
<i> You're so slow.</i>

317
00:17:19,333 --> 00:17:22,033
<i>- Wait, wait.
- The base.</i>

318
00:17:22,167 --> 00:17:23,200
<i> Hi, guys.</i>

319
00:17:23,333 --> 00:17:24,733
<i>Just one more sale
and we're done.</i>

320
00:17:24,867 --> 00:17:26,733
<i>We have tickets here
for the Siklab concert...</i>

321
00:17:26,867 --> 00:17:28,300
<i>- Disaster streak.
- Go ahead.</i>

322
00:17:28,433 --> 00:17:30,133
<i> Just comment now, guys.</i>

323
00:17:30,267 --> 00:17:31,167
<i> Come on.</i>

324
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:32,800
<i> No fake buyers, okay?</i>

325
00:17:32,933 --> 00:17:34,200
<i>- Come on, claim them now.
- The base.</i>

326
00:17:34,333 --> 00:17:36,400
Those are the only tickets left.

327
00:17:36,533 --> 00:17:38,100
[CELLPHONE CHIMES]

328
00:17:38,233 --> 00:17:39,733
<i> It's Mr. Moon.</i>

329
00:17:39,867 --> 00:17:41,133
<i> Mr. Moon.</i>

330
00:17:41,267 --> 00:17:42,533
<i> Mr. Moon, hi.</i>

331
00:17:42,667 --> 00:17:44,633
<i>- Hi, Mr. Moon.
- Are you for real, Calix?</i>

332
00:17:44,767 --> 00:17:46,233
<i> Seriously?</i>

333
00:17:46,367 --> 00:17:48,533
<i>Why are you buying
Angel's ticket?</i>

334
00:17:48,700 --> 00:17:50,433
<i> Shut up, Raviel.</i>

335
00:17:50,567 --> 00:17:52,200
<i>Someone might hear you,
Poncy and Dash are right there.</i>

336
00:17:52,333 --> 00:17:53,433
<i>- Thank you.
- Thank you, Mr. Moon.</i>

337
00:17:53,567 --> 00:17:55,100
<i> Just send us a message.</i>

338
00:17:55,233 --> 00:17:57,567
<i> So? Why?</i>

339
00:17:57,700 --> 00:18:01,100
<i>Why are you helping
our nemesis?</i>

340
00:18:01,767 --> 00:18:02,933
<i> It doesn't make sense.</i>

341
00:18:04,867 --> 00:18:09,233
<i>If she loses her grandfather,
she'll lose her drive to study.</i>

342
00:18:09,367 --> 00:18:10,233
<i> Hey, hey, there it is!</i>

343
00:18:10,367 --> 00:18:11,233
<i> Hey!</i>

344
00:18:11,367 --> 00:18:13,600
<i>And I want her to continue
studying.</i>

345
00:18:13,733 --> 00:18:15,833
[RAVIEL LAUGHS]

346
00:18:15,967 --> 00:18:18,133
<i>This is the first time I've been
challenged like this, Raviel.</i>

347
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:23,267
<i> Don't tell me you're...</i>

348
00:18:23,433 --> 00:18:24,533
<i> Wait.</i>

349
00:18:24,667 --> 00:18:27,833
<i>Don't tell me you're falling
for that freak.</i>

350
00:18:27,967 --> 00:18:29,767
<i>- Are you?
- Say that again.</i>

351
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:30,967
<i> You're falling for that freak.</i>

352
00:18:31,100 --> 00:18:32,700
<i>Why would I ever fall for Angel?</i>

353
00:18:35,333 --> 00:18:36,367
<i> Hey, that's not allowed.</i>

354
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:37,900
<i>Don't forget your place, Raviel.</i>

355
00:18:44,100 --> 00:18:49,100
<i>You swear to me,
no one can ever know about this,</i>

356
00:18:49,233 --> 00:18:50,200
<i> no one.</i>

357
00:18:53,700 --> 00:18:55,233
<i> Of course.</i>

358
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:56,233
<i> Of course, Calix.</i>

359
00:18:57,933 --> 00:18:59,033
<i> Of course.</i>

360
00:18:59,167 --> 00:19:00,400
<i> Of course, Calix.</i>

361
00:19:00,533 --> 00:19:01,533
<i> I got you.</i>

362
00:19:03,867 --> 00:19:05,100
<i> No worries.</i>

363
00:19:32,100 --> 00:19:35,433
I bought a game skin, Mom.

364
00:19:36,967 --> 00:19:41,967
So that explains your
embarrassing drop in standards,

365
00:19:42,100 --> 00:19:43,633
your academic decline.

366
00:19:43,767 --> 00:19:44,933
[TENSE MUSIC]

367
00:19:45,067 --> 00:19:46,467
You're grounded.

368
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:48,067
No games for a month.

369
00:19:49,367 --> 00:19:51,367
Try to keep up with
your brothers, Calix.

370
00:19:52,867 --> 00:19:56,233
You're already only half
an Arcilla,

371
00:19:56,367 --> 00:19:58,567
so don't become an even greater
disgrace to our family.

372
00:20:03,833 --> 00:20:06,600
Andrei, how's school?

373
00:20:06,733 --> 00:20:09,400
Well, I'm doing fine, Mom,
as always.

374
00:20:09,533 --> 00:20:11,367
I might not qualify anymore

375
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:12,933
because I think I'm only
on the Dean's List, Mom.

376
00:20:13,067 --> 00:20:13,867
Wow.

377
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:15,300
My son is truly exceptional.

378
00:20:15,433 --> 00:20:17,967
So, do you want to stop
by my office later?

379
00:20:18,100 --> 00:20:18,967
Let's have lunch.

380
00:20:19,100 --> 00:20:19,700
Sure, Mom.

381
00:20:31,667 --> 00:20:33,167
According to our people,

382
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:35,667
your father was reportedly going
in and out of the hospital

383
00:20:35,833 --> 00:20:38,533
before they came here
to Solmera City.

384
00:20:38,667 --> 00:20:40,500
I'll find out
what illness he has.

385
00:20:40,633 --> 00:20:42,167
No, Tyrone.

386
00:20:42,300 --> 00:20:44,000
I don't care about my father.

387
00:20:45,867 --> 00:20:50,033
What I want to know is
who that girl is at the resort,

388
00:20:50,167 --> 00:20:51,667
that Angel.

389
00:20:51,800 --> 00:20:54,067
That's what I need an update on.

390
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:55,867
Don't stress yourself out.

391
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:57,300
I found something
about that too.

392
00:21:01,533 --> 00:21:02,900
Apparently, Beverly adopted her.

393
00:21:04,500 --> 00:21:05,867
Adopted?

394
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,100
Seriously?

395
00:21:08,300 --> 00:21:11,000
I'm just not sure about
the circumstances

396
00:21:11,167 --> 00:21:12,600
of where she came from.

397
00:21:18,267 --> 00:21:21,833
And yet, they loved her so much.

398
00:21:23,400 --> 00:21:25,367
While I...

399
00:21:25,500 --> 00:21:27,067
all I ever got was blame.

400
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:29,600
I was even holding
my baby back then.

401
00:21:31,700 --> 00:21:36,100
I also found out that Angel
is exceptionally intelligent.

402
00:21:36,233 --> 00:21:38,933
She's supposedly the reason they
were able to build that resort.

403
00:21:40,300 --> 00:21:42,567
Find out what else there
is to know about this girl

404
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:47,700
because I'm going to
destroy her life.

405
00:21:53,567 --> 00:21:56,567
<i>Coming up tomorrow
on You're My Favorite Song...</i>

406
00:21:56,700 --> 00:21:59,033
Why did you destroy our resort?

407
00:21:59,167 --> 00:22:00,667
Did someone order you to do it,

408
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:02,033
or are you just a bunch of
good-for-nothing troublemakers

409
00:22:02,167 --> 00:22:03,967
with nothing better to do?

410
00:22:04,100 --> 00:22:06,333
What? Who?

411
00:22:06,467 --> 00:22:10,667
Welcome to Gran Vista Resort,
everybody.

412
00:22:10,800 --> 00:22:12,167
[GUESTS APPLAUDING]

413
00:22:12,300 --> 00:22:14,033
Hey. What's the question?

414
00:22:14,167 --> 00:22:15,033
Bring it on.

415
00:22:16,667 --> 00:22:19,267
So, Calix, do you have feelings
for Angel?

416
00:22:20,933 --> 00:22:23,233
We need to meet
Mr. Moon tomorrow.

417
00:22:23,367 --> 00:22:25,233
He's picking up the tickets
for Siklab.

418
00:22:25,500 --> 00:22:26,533
Okay.

419
00:22:26,667 --> 00:22:30,233
I'd like to meet him too
and I want to thank him.

420
00:22:30,367 --> 00:22:32,333
So, it's you.

421
00:22:32,467 --> 00:22:35,367
Angel of Gran Vista Resort.

422
00:22:35,500 --> 00:22:39,333
I'm Serina of the
Montaverde Group of Hotels.

423
00:22:39,467 --> 00:22:42,700
I want you and your family
out of Solmera City.

424
00:22:42,833 --> 00:22:44,767
I want your resort
to go bankrupt

425
00:22:44,900 --> 00:22:47,200
so I can buy it
for the Montaverde Empire.

426
00:22:50,100 --> 00:22:51,500
Look what you did, you little...

427
00:22:51,633 --> 00:22:54,433
[TENSE MUSIC]

428
00:22:56,267 --> 00:22:57,200
Young lady.

429
00:22:59,633 --> 00:23:00,800
Are you okay?

430
00:23:00,933 --> 00:23:05,867
[HOPEFUL MUSIC]
